<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rai Sahasi II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 632</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rai Sahasi II was the last king of the Rai dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chach-nama">Chach Nama</a>. After his death, his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> chamberlain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Chach</a> married his widow and seized the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aror">Aror</a> around 632, founding the Brahman dynasty that ruled Sindh until the Arab conquest of 711–712.</p></div>
